  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A proton and an <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>-particle are accelerated from rest by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> potentials, respectively. The ratio of their de-Broglie wavelength is :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the de Broglie wavelength of the proton is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>V</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the de Broglie wavelength of the alpha particle is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mi>V</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide equation (1) by equation (2) and simplify to obtain the required ratio.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></msqrt><msqrt><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mi>V</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (3) to calculate the required ratio.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msqrt><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
